WEBVTT


00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:01.580
Factory works in this loop

00:00:01.581 --> 00:00:05.081
a feature comes through the spec writer which goes into the builder,

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:08.840
which then gets verified by various review agents

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.660
and once those are done, if we need changes,

00:00:11.661 --> 00:00:14.301
this happens in a loop and then we go to the approver

00:00:14.302 --> 00:00:18.681
which either merges to main the feature or we get a human review.

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.900
And this is a system we can use repeatedly

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:24.021
every time we wanna build a new feature for our project.

00:00:24.022 --> 00:00:26.141
And we could imagine in the future we want you know,

00:00:26.142 --> 00:00:28.541
we can bring in data sources from the outside world.

00:00:28.542 --> 00:00:31.081
Let's see if our factory can handle this feature

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:32.580
inside my actual website.

00:00:32.581 --> 00:00:34.781
This is my production site that we're working in right now.

00:00:34.782 --> 00:00:37.381
And now we can see we're starting to use our subagents.

00:00:37.382 --> 00:00:38.141
Here's the first one.

00:00:38.142 --> 00:00:41.341
We're creating a spec using the spec writer background agent

00:00:41.342 --> 00:00:45.021
and I can see our builder has just started working on this. Okay,

00:00:45.022 --> 00:00:46.801
sweet. We just went to review

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:49.420
and we just kicked off all of our review subagents.

00:00:49.421 --> 00:00:52.021
So these guys are representing our review.

00:00:52.022 --> 00:00:52.901
They're doing it. Okay,

00:00:52.902 --> 00:00:57.301
the UX round finished the UI round finished and they passed.

00:00:57.302 --> 00:01:00.421
But we're doing the security over here considering. Okay,

00:01:00.422 --> 00:01:03.001
that's done code review. This is this is epic.

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:03.780
Oh, look at this

00:01:03.781 --> 00:01:06.541
you guys. We can even see the little icons.

00:01:06.542 --> 00:01:09.461
It's deciding if this feature should be pulled in or not.

00:01:09.462 --> 00:01:10.701
I'm actually blown away.

00:01:10.702 --> 00:01:14.041
This is this is How I want to develop features now.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.940
Why have I not done this yet?

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:18.581
So what's Opus deciding? It's escalating.

00:01:18.582 --> 00:01:20.761
So I think it'll go to the human review.

00:01:20.762 --> 00:01:23.781
There it is. So it's sitting in the human review phase.

00:01:23.782 --> 00:01:25.301
And now I need to approve this.

00:01:25.302 --> 00:01:27.861
Click on this. Okay.

00:01:27.862 --> 00:01:30.941
I can get all sorts of information from the dashboard.

00:01:30.942 --> 00:01:33.021
Escalate, why the build is clean,

00:01:33.022 --> 00:01:35.681
every acceptance criteria for the human,

00:01:36.060 --> 00:01:36.880
if both.

00:01:37.580 --> 00:01:39.220
So here's how I would approve it.

00:01:39.221 --> 00:01:41.841
I would need to know the ID of this feature

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:44.460
